  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than an administrative error or information request. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P review is the appropriate next step to challenge the bundling determination. Resubmitting the same claim would likely result in another denial or a duplicate claim error, and an appeal is premature before exhausting the P2P option.",
